codex
Projection tuning shows a meaningful small-shape improvement with `BLOCK_M=64, BLOCK_H=32, num_warps=4`; the current code only uses that style for `N=768`. I’m waiting for the large-shape results because this may be a good shape-specific rule for `N=256` or `N=512`.
